1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:10,001
<font color="#ffff00">Provided by explosiveskull</font>
https://twitter.com/kaboomskull

2
00:02:26,388 --> 00:02:29,517
This film was inspired by real events

3
00:02:55,125 --> 00:02:57,377
I greet you, O my sister.

4
00:03:00,255 --> 00:03:01,882
You want to sing her a song?

5
00:03:25,906 --> 00:03:26,949
What's your business?

6
00:03:28,033 --> 00:03:31,161
We're going to Pescia
for my daughter to take the veil.

7
00:03:31,244 --> 00:03:33,664
They must carry silver coin, captain.

8
00:03:33,747 --> 00:03:34,998
The convent dowry.

9
00:03:35,082 --> 00:03:37,084
I have promissory notes, not silver!

10
00:03:37,417 --> 00:03:39,336
You have something worth taking!

11
00:03:46,134 --> 00:03:47,302
Give that back!

12
00:03:47,678 --> 00:03:48,971
It's my mother's.

13
00:03:50,097 --> 00:03:51,849
She has bigger balls than you!

14
00:03:52,182 --> 00:03:54,101
The Blessed Virgin will punish you.

15
00:03:54,351 --> 00:03:56,019
How do you know, child?

16
00:03:56,103 --> 00:03:57,980
She does all I ask of her.

17
00:03:58,230 --> 00:03:59,439
She can go to hell,

18
00:03:59,898 --> 00:04:00,858
your Virgin!

19
00:04:02,109 --> 00:04:03,110
You hear that?

20
00:04:03,944 --> 00:04:05,445
The Virgin's voice.

21
00:04:06,112 --> 00:04:07,280
To prove she heard me.

22
00:04:13,454 --> 00:04:14,412
Shit!

23
00:04:16,373 --> 00:04:17,332
Here!

24
00:04:17,666 --> 00:04:19,918
The Blessed Virgin
will have fun with you!

25
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:21,169
Forward!

26
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,394
Good day, Signor Carlini.

27
00:05:20,228 --> 00:05:21,897
If you'd care to follow me.

28
00:05:30,405 --> 00:05:31,364
Wait here.

29
00:05:36,995 --> 00:05:40,874
The Theatines are grateful
for your bringing Jesus a new bride.

30
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,669
Benedetta will be happy here.

31
00:05:43,752 --> 00:05:47,631
I also bring oranges, apples and wine
in significant quantities.

32
00:05:47,715 --> 00:05:50,676
For the next 25 years,
you will receive the same.

33
00:05:50,759 --> 00:05:51,802
Every year.

34
00:05:53,053 --> 00:05:56,056
That is very generous of you,
Signor Carlini.

35
00:05:56,515 --> 00:05:58,308
And for the dowry?

36
00:06:02,187 --> 00:06:05,398
When my Benedetta was born,
she almost died.

37
00:06:05,483 --> 00:06:07,400
By miracle, God saved her.

38
00:06:07,485 --> 00:06:09,027
I pledged her to him.

39
00:06:09,528 --> 00:06:11,196
A very moving story.

40
00:06:11,404 --> 00:06:13,198
I have heard many like it.

41
00:06:13,406 --> 00:06:14,992
Each time, I am touched.

42
00:06:15,826 --> 00:06:16,994
But every year,

43
00:06:17,077 --> 00:06:20,539
we receive hundreds of girls,
who want to serve God.

44
00:06:21,373 --> 00:06:23,000
This year's candidates.

45
00:06:23,501 --> 00:06:25,210
And I can only take three.

46
00:06:27,254 --> 00:06:29,256
Aware of the challenges you face,

47
00:06:29,339 --> 00:06:32,217
I'd be delighted to donate 50 gold scudi.

48
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:35,012
The fruit and wine
might also count for something.

49
00:06:35,095 --> 00:06:36,304
Am I right?

50
00:06:36,388 --> 00:06:37,765
Beyond these walls,

51
00:06:37,848 --> 00:06:41,184
a bride's dowry
never descends below 150 scudi.

52
00:06:41,977 --> 00:06:45,648
Is a bride of Christ
worth less than a hundred?

53
00:06:47,733 --> 00:06:49,777
Let's split the difference. 75!

54
00:06:50,694 --> 00:06:53,030
You'd haggle like a Jew
over 25 scudi?

55
00:06:53,113 --> 00:06:55,949
After all, Giuliano,
she's your beloved daughter.

56
00:06:57,701 --> 00:06:58,702
Agreed.

57
00:06:59,787 --> 00:07:00,746
100 scudi.

58
00:07:00,829 --> 00:07:03,206
We are not horse-trading.

59
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:04,708
Your word is enough.

60
00:07:05,125 --> 00:07:07,044
And your promissory note.

61
00:07:19,306 --> 00:07:20,265
Too big.

62
00:07:23,477 --> 00:07:25,563
- They're so beautiful.
- Undress!

63
00:07:28,065 --> 00:07:29,525
Who gave you that?

64
00:07:29,608 --> 00:07:30,776
My mother.

65
00:07:30,859 --> 00:07:32,486
For me to pray to the Blessed Virgin.

66
00:07:33,904 --> 00:07:36,532
Child, the convent has its own Virgin.

67
00:07:36,615 --> 00:07:38,742
From now on, you'll pray to her.

68
00:07:38,826 --> 00:07:40,869
- But she's mine!
- Come on, hurry.

69
00:07:41,495 --> 00:07:42,580
Undress now.

70
00:07:49,878 --> 00:07:51,714
It's so itchy, it's horrible.

71
00:07:52,130 --> 00:07:53,340
As it should be.

72
00:07:54,091 --> 00:07:55,843
Your worst enemy is your body.

73
00:07:56,176 --> 00:07:58,512
Best not to feel at home in it.

74
00:08:04,518 --> 00:08:06,520
When I was barely older than you,

75
00:08:06,895 --> 00:08:10,190
I lost two inches of flesh
to a drunkard's knife.

76
00:08:10,608 --> 00:08:14,111
This wooden finger is dearer to me
than the other nine.

77
00:08:14,987 --> 00:08:18,281
If I could,
I'd replace every part of my body,

78
00:08:18,907 --> 00:08:20,909
until I was a block of wood,

79
00:08:20,993 --> 00:08:23,496
carved with the name of God.

80
00:08:25,581 --> 00:08:27,249
Like a gravestone?

81
00:08:30,961 --> 00:08:32,545
You're an intelligent girl.

82
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,799
But intelligence can be dangerous, child.

83
00:08:36,717 --> 00:08:38,135
And not only for others.

84
00:08:48,311 --> 00:08:49,980
Benedetta, this way.

85
00:08:58,030 --> 00:08:59,281
Give me that.

86
00:09:04,286 --> 00:09:05,496
This is your cell.

87
00:09:11,752 --> 00:09:12,920
Wear this tomorrow.

88
00:09:56,379 --> 00:09:57,590
My beloved Mary,

89
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:59,800
you are my mother now.

90
00:10:00,676 --> 00:10:02,302
I pray thee, help me.

91
00:10:02,385 --> 00:10:03,637
I feel so alone.

92
00:10:04,763 --> 00:10:06,724
Do you even hear me
from where I am?

93
00:10:21,947 --> 00:10:22,906
Benedetta!

94
00:10:24,992 --> 00:10:26,076
Are you hurt?

95
00:10:27,202 --> 00:10:28,411
Raise the statue!

96
00:10:36,294 --> 00:10:37,880
- Did you touch it?
- No!

97
00:10:37,963 --> 00:10:39,882
Something snapped and it fell.

98
00:10:39,965 --> 00:10:40,966
Why were you here?

99
00:10:41,925 --> 00:10:43,761
I wanted to pray to the Virgin.

100
00:10:45,387 --> 00:10:47,347
Can your legs hold you?

101
00:10:49,057 --> 00:10:50,017
Yes.

102
00:10:51,977 --> 00:10:54,062
It's a miracle she wasn't crushed.

103
00:10:57,232 --> 00:11:00,235
Well, go back to bed
and take Benedetta to hers.

104
00:11:01,236 --> 00:11:02,195
Come.

105
00:11:08,243 --> 00:11:09,202
Mother!

106
00:11:11,163 --> 00:11:12,998
Could it be a real miracle?

107
00:11:13,499 --> 00:11:15,543
Let's not have loose talk.

108
00:11:15,626 --> 00:11:17,711
Miracles sprout like mushrooms,

109
00:11:17,795 --> 00:11:20,964
and usually they're more trouble
than they're worth.

110
00:11:21,048 --> 00:11:22,633
I didn't really believe it.

111
00:11:27,596 --> 00:11:30,891
18 years later

112
00:11:31,767 --> 00:11:34,436
I so desired to see my son,
the Lord Jesus.

113
00:11:35,604 --> 00:11:38,273
I so desired
his bodily presence once more.

114
00:11:38,816 --> 00:11:39,858
Then God,

115
00:11:40,818 --> 00:11:44,071
in his infinite generosity,
sent me an angel,

116
00:11:44,154 --> 00:11:45,656
who proclaimed this night,

117
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:49,034
"You shall ascend to your son in glory!"

118
00:11:51,161 --> 00:11:53,872
To have your company here, my brothers,

119
00:11:54,289 --> 00:11:55,916
I have fervently prayed.

120
00:11:55,999 --> 00:11:57,334
Noble lady,

121
00:11:57,417 --> 00:11:59,587
full of grace and wisdom,

122
00:11:59,670 --> 00:12:01,296
you are our reward.

123
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:09,763
Now I shall lay in this bed,
arrayed here for me.

124
00:13:10,533 --> 00:13:11,492
Benedetta!

125
00:13:14,912 --> 00:13:15,871
Come!

126
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:17,748
You are my wife!

127
00:13:19,542 --> 00:13:20,584
Come to me!

128
00:13:22,795 --> 00:13:24,004
I'm coming, Lord.

129
00:13:24,087 --> 00:13:25,088
I'm coming!

130
00:13:26,006 --> 00:13:27,049
Come to me!

131
00:13:36,475 --> 00:13:37,893
Benedetta, your feet!

132
00:13:57,955 --> 00:14:01,249
This feast is a gift
from our generous guest,

133
00:14:01,333 --> 00:14:03,001
Giulano Carlini.

134
00:14:03,085 --> 00:14:04,753
Let us drink to his health.

135
00:14:08,381 --> 00:14:12,470
A thought for our dear bishop of Milan,
taken from us last week.

136
00:14:13,804 --> 00:14:16,014
I heard it was the plague.

137
00:14:17,307 --> 00:14:18,266
Indeed.

138
00:14:19,727 --> 00:14:21,562
The bishop was a good man.

139
00:14:24,106 --> 00:14:27,359
But I always thought his cathedral
turned his head.

140
00:14:28,944 --> 00:14:30,613
If it pleases God,

141
00:14:30,696 --> 00:14:33,741
the bishop's seat
will better fit your Grace.

142
00:14:33,824 --> 00:14:34,783
No.

143
00:14:35,868 --> 00:14:37,035
And it is sad.

144
00:14:37,536 --> 00:14:41,665
Despite courting the Vatican
with the impudence of a harlot,

145
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:45,002
I am quite simply not conspicuous enough.

146
00:14:46,044 --> 00:14:50,173
It would be a prodigy if the Pope
could locate Pescia on a map.

147
00:14:50,257 --> 00:14:53,927
So let us hope
for a cartographic miracle.

148
00:15:01,309 --> 00:15:03,061
Why were you moving your feet?

149
00:15:03,854 --> 00:15:05,648
You were supposed to be dead.

150
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:09,067
I saw Jesus.

151
00:15:10,653 --> 00:15:11,862
He came to me.

152
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:16,992
I'm his bride, am I not?

153
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:19,077
Yes, of course.

154
00:15:23,331 --> 00:15:24,708
Open the door!

155
00:15:25,834 --> 00:15:26,919
Open it.

156
00:15:27,002 --> 00:15:29,087
He'll kill me! Help me!

157
00:15:30,088 --> 00:15:31,757
Open up! Please!

158
00:15:38,889 --> 00:15:40,933
Take me! No, he's coming!

159
00:15:41,016 --> 00:15:42,059
Please, help!

160
00:15:42,142 --> 00:15:43,143
Harlot!

161
00:15:43,477 --> 00:15:44,436
You can't escape!

162
00:15:44,937 --> 00:15:46,564
You're mine, little whore!

163
00:15:46,939 --> 00:15:47,898
Let me stay!

164
00:15:47,981 --> 00:15:48,941
Please!

165
00:15:50,693 --> 00:15:51,652
Come on!

166
00:15:53,571 --> 00:15:55,113
You're looking for a fight?

167
00:15:55,197 --> 00:15:56,615
This is a convent.

168
00:15:59,076 --> 00:16:01,119
I love Jesus.
Take me.

169
00:16:01,203 --> 00:16:02,788
I'm her father.
She belongs to me.

170
00:16:02,871 --> 00:16:04,498
Let me stay here.

171
00:16:06,041 --> 00:16:08,502
A convent
is not a place of charity, child.

172
00:16:08,586 --> 00:16:10,295
You must pay to come here.

173
00:16:10,378 --> 00:16:11,755
Do you have money?

174
00:16:12,255 --> 00:16:13,256
No.

175
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:15,092
Enough now. That's enough!

176
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:17,595
Let me go.

177
00:16:17,678 --> 00:16:18,929
I want to serve God.

178
00:16:20,138 --> 00:16:22,224
- Mother, help her!
- We'll pay.

179
00:16:23,183 --> 00:16:24,602
Pay a stranger's dowry?

180
00:16:25,018 --> 00:16:27,229
I'll pray my whole life for you, sire.

181
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:28,856
Magnificent!

182
00:16:29,815 --> 00:16:30,941
Signor Carlini,

183
00:16:31,525 --> 00:16:33,902
the rich do not enter
the kingdom of God.

184
00:16:34,862 --> 00:16:35,904
Jesus said so.

185
00:16:36,864 --> 00:16:39,449
Reverend Mother,
you have devoted yourself

186
00:16:39,533 --> 00:16:40,784
to ensuring my entry.

187
00:16:43,161 --> 00:16:44,162
Very well.

188
00:16:45,122 --> 00:16:46,874
A gift for you, Benedetta.

189
00:16:48,959 --> 00:16:51,962
What gift?
You won't get my daughter for nothing.

190
00:16:52,045 --> 00:16:53,088
Not on your life!

191
00:16:53,171 --> 00:16:54,798
10 dinari, no more.

192
00:16:54,881 --> 00:16:58,051
20. And the price of a good dog
to replace the slut.

193
00:17:24,828 --> 00:17:25,788
There.

194
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:27,748
That's delicious.

195
00:17:29,416 --> 00:17:30,417
Here, catch.

196
00:17:34,672 --> 00:17:35,798
Soap yourself well.

197
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:38,091
What's your name?

198
00:17:38,676 --> 00:17:40,010
Sister Benedetta. And you?

199
00:17:40,427 --> 00:17:41,386
Bartolomea.

200
00:17:42,429 --> 00:17:43,556
Bartolomea what?

201
00:17:44,014 --> 00:17:45,390
Bartolomea nothing.

202
00:17:45,974 --> 00:17:47,560
Washing well is a rule?

203
00:17:47,643 --> 00:17:49,603
A clean soul demands a clean body.

204
00:17:49,687 --> 00:17:51,396
I scrub as hard as I can.

205
00:17:51,855 --> 00:17:53,982
Shit, my soap. Where is it?

206
00:17:56,569 --> 00:17:57,528
I nearly fell.

207
00:17:58,946 --> 00:18:00,864
Is any water left so I can rinse?

208
00:18:02,658 --> 00:18:03,701
Sister Benedetta?

209
00:18:05,368 --> 00:18:07,162
Your nightgown is on the table.

210
00:18:21,844 --> 00:18:23,011
Sister Benedetta?

211
00:18:23,679 --> 00:18:25,473
To take a shit, where do I go?

212
00:18:30,644 --> 00:18:31,687
Follow me.

213
00:18:36,484 --> 00:18:37,610
Real commodes?

214
00:18:38,486 --> 00:18:41,697
- Where did you do it?
- Outside. With the animals.

215
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:56,294
That's so good! What a relief!

216
00:18:56,587 --> 00:18:58,881
We must not talk so loudly at night.

217
00:19:01,216 --> 00:19:02,801
That's allowed, I hope.

218
00:19:04,595 --> 00:19:05,554
Wait.

219
00:19:19,359 --> 00:19:20,819
Forgive me, who did that?

220
00:19:21,319 --> 00:19:22,362
My father.

221
00:19:22,821 --> 00:19:23,781
Why?

222
00:19:26,324 --> 00:19:28,243
The plague took mama last year,

223
00:19:28,326 --> 00:19:30,663
so my father made me his wife.

224
00:19:33,666 --> 00:19:35,042
I always told him no.

225
00:19:35,125 --> 00:19:37,503
He always told me
he didn't give a damn.

226
00:19:38,712 --> 00:19:41,256
- His wife for everything?
- Yes, everything.

227
00:19:42,174 --> 00:19:44,843
My brothers did the same behind his back.

228
00:19:47,345 --> 00:19:50,348
This morning,
I tried to stick him with scissors.

229
00:19:51,391 --> 00:19:52,976
For that, he massacred me.

230
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,853
That's why I ran away.

231
00:19:58,691 --> 00:20:00,651
Beauty is not always an advantage.

232
00:20:00,734 --> 00:20:02,778
If I were a goat, he'd do the same.

233
00:20:04,071 --> 00:20:05,072
I'm beautiful?

234
00:20:07,616 --> 00:20:09,242
You mean you don't know?

235
00:20:11,495 --> 00:20:13,371
No, we never had a mirror.

236
00:20:15,165 --> 00:20:16,208
You are beautiful.

237
00:20:17,375 --> 00:20:19,127
View your reflection in my eyes.

238
00:20:24,883 --> 00:20:26,051
I see nothing.

239
00:20:26,134 --> 00:20:27,385
You have to be closer.

240
00:20:31,974 --> 00:20:33,183
You see yourself?

241
00:20:36,687 --> 00:20:38,230
What are you two doing?

242
00:20:41,108 --> 00:20:43,235
She didn't know where the privy was.

243
00:20:50,283 --> 00:20:51,368
Who's she?

244
00:20:51,952 --> 00:20:54,538
Christina, our Reverend Mother's daughter.

245
00:20:54,622 --> 00:20:56,915
And she spies for her mother?

246
00:21:21,857 --> 00:21:25,193
Holy Mother, I believe
Sister Bartolomea seeks my guidance

247
00:21:25,277 --> 00:21:27,154
but I am not worthy to teach her.

248
00:21:28,781 --> 00:21:31,324
<i>God himself put this girl in your path.</i>

249
00:21:31,408 --> 00:21:34,369
<i>Is she not in need of love and advice?</i>

250
00:21:35,871 --> 00:21:39,041
Yes, but she must be directed
with a strong hand.

251
00:21:39,124 --> 00:21:40,375
Which I lack.

252
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:43,253
<i>God will show the way.</i>

253
00:22:49,778 --> 00:22:51,446
Help me! Jesus!

254
00:23:02,833 --> 00:23:04,376
What did these beasts want?

255
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:05,461
To kill you.

256
00:23:06,253 --> 00:23:09,381
They were demons,
trying to keep us apart.

257
00:23:10,007 --> 00:23:11,467
But they are stupid.

258
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:14,762
Neither life, nor death can separate us.

259
00:23:26,189 --> 00:23:27,315
Stay with me.

260
00:23:28,484 --> 00:23:29,777
Yes, sweet Jesus.

261
00:23:34,782 --> 00:23:36,074
I'll stay with you.

262
00:24:20,536 --> 00:24:21,745
Speak, sister.

263
00:24:22,996 --> 00:24:23,997
Father...

264
00:24:25,749 --> 00:24:26,917
I have seen Jesus.

265
00:24:28,627 --> 00:24:29,712
In a dream?

266
00:24:29,795 --> 00:24:30,754
No.

267
00:24:32,297 --> 00:24:33,466
In the flesh.

268
00:24:34,049 --> 00:24:35,634
As I see you before me now.

269
00:24:38,471 --> 00:24:40,180
Seeing him, what did you feel?

270
00:24:42,349 --> 00:24:44,935
- Fear.
- Then it was a false vision.

271
00:24:45,728 --> 00:24:48,313
A true manifestation of Christ
fills us with joy.

272
00:24:51,024 --> 00:24:52,985
How can I know what is true or false?

273
00:24:55,738 --> 00:24:57,114
Through suffering.

274
00:24:57,322 --> 00:25:00,075
Suffering is the only way to know Christ.

275
00:25:02,495 --> 00:25:05,122
I know God wants us to suffer but...

276
00:25:07,458 --> 00:25:09,042
- It frightens me.
- Naturally.

277
00:25:10,335 --> 00:25:12,045
The ways of the Lord are often terrifying.

278
00:25:12,921 --> 00:25:14,715
Imbeciles say,

279
00:25:14,798 --> 00:25:17,468
"I do not fear him
for I know he is good."

280
00:25:18,469 --> 00:25:20,763
Have they never seen a surgeon at work?

281
00:25:23,223 --> 00:25:25,559
So we must welcome affliction?

282
00:25:25,976 --> 00:25:27,728
Pray that it shall come.

283
00:25:29,688 --> 00:25:31,815
<i>Ego te absolvo.</i>

284
00:25:51,043 --> 00:25:53,796
The bobbins are ruined.
You know their value?

285
00:25:54,505 --> 00:25:56,507
- You idiot!
- You ran into me!

286
00:25:57,049 --> 00:25:58,175
Pardon me?

287
00:25:58,258 --> 00:25:59,426
It's your fault.

288
00:25:59,510 --> 00:26:00,553
Stop lying.

289
00:26:02,179 --> 00:26:03,305
It was you.

290
00:26:05,015 --> 00:26:06,433
Take the bobbins out.

291
00:26:06,934 --> 00:26:08,393
The water is boiling.

292
00:26:09,728 --> 00:26:12,230
Quickly,
or you go back to your father.

293
00:26:36,004 --> 00:26:37,339
Now, the rest.

294
00:26:39,633 --> 00:26:40,968
I must do it again?

295
00:26:41,384 --> 00:26:43,637
While we talk, the bobbins break.

296
00:26:47,057 --> 00:26:48,016
Stop!

297
00:26:48,100 --> 00:26:49,142
Well then?

298
00:26:50,102 --> 00:26:51,604
What is this now?

299
00:26:54,189 --> 00:26:56,149
Bartolomea burned her hand.

300
00:26:57,985 --> 00:26:59,111
Back to work!

301
00:26:59,194 --> 00:27:02,197
Sister Petra,
she needs to go to the infirmary.

302
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:03,406
Take her.

303
00:27:11,164 --> 00:27:14,417
I hear one of your sisters
damaged bobbins of silk

304
00:27:14,502 --> 00:27:16,712
and you took it upon yourself

305
00:27:16,795 --> 00:27:18,506
to administer punishment.

306
00:27:18,589 --> 00:27:19,715
No, Reverend Mother.

307
00:27:22,801 --> 00:27:23,802
No?

308
00:27:23,886 --> 00:27:26,138
My aim was not to punish
but to hurt her.

309
00:27:27,264 --> 00:27:30,058
You wanted to inflict pain on your sister?

310
00:27:30,142 --> 00:27:31,351
Deliberately?

311
00:27:31,434 --> 00:27:32,770
Yes, deliberately.

312
00:27:33,521 --> 00:27:35,397
There was no malice in it?

313
00:27:36,857 --> 00:27:39,610
If you say it was malice,
I'll know it to be true.

314
00:27:39,818 --> 00:27:42,029
You don't know your own feelings?

315
00:27:43,656 --> 00:27:44,865
It seems not.

316
00:27:56,001 --> 00:27:58,921
Did Bartolomea do something to anger you?

317
00:27:59,630 --> 00:28:00,631
No.

318
00:28:00,714 --> 00:28:02,883
Do you detest her for some reason?

319
00:28:02,966 --> 00:28:03,926
No!

320
00:28:08,263 --> 00:28:10,724
Do you feel affection for her?

321
00:28:14,311 --> 00:28:15,312
I feel...

322
00:28:15,896 --> 00:28:17,523
compassion, yes.

323
00:28:17,981 --> 00:28:19,274
For all her sufferings.

324
00:28:19,608 --> 00:28:21,610
Including those you inflict?

325
00:28:22,027 --> 00:28:24,822
Father Ricordati says
sufferings guide us to God

326
00:28:24,905 --> 00:28:26,490
and make us stronger.

327
00:28:27,783 --> 00:28:29,201
Our own sufferings.

328
00:28:30,410 --> 00:28:31,829
Not the sufferings of others.

329
00:28:36,291 --> 00:28:37,751
You were overzealous.

330
00:28:37,835 --> 00:28:39,712
You'll go without bread for a week,

331
00:28:39,795 --> 00:28:43,215
and for two weeks,
you'll change Sister Jacopa's bedding.

332
00:28:43,298 --> 00:28:44,842
You may go.

333
00:28:44,925 --> 00:28:46,218
Yes, Reverend Mother.

334
00:29:10,033 --> 00:29:11,034
I'm here to help.

335
00:29:11,409 --> 00:29:14,037
Stay back!
I take pride in my suffering.

336
00:29:15,413 --> 00:29:16,999
Pride is a mortal sin.

337
00:29:19,042 --> 00:29:21,044
We're all entitled to a sin.

338
00:29:22,671 --> 00:29:23,631
What's yours?

339
00:29:25,423 --> 00:29:26,759
I have never sinned.

340
00:29:29,094 --> 00:29:30,971
But I could at any moment.

341
00:29:31,054 --> 00:29:32,014
Of course.

342
00:29:33,641 --> 00:29:34,642
Help me.

343
00:29:37,269 --> 00:29:38,479
My sin is,

344
00:29:39,146 --> 00:29:40,689
I was born a Jew.

345
00:29:42,274 --> 00:29:43,942
Sister Petra was a whore.

346
00:29:44,026 --> 00:29:46,904
Selling herself in privies in Florence.
Nobody cares.

347
00:29:48,238 --> 00:29:50,699
But my father's prick was circumcised.

348
00:29:51,742 --> 00:29:54,953
And that fault is unforgivable.

349
00:30:07,591 --> 00:30:09,802
You've discovered my secret lover.

350
00:30:12,095 --> 00:30:13,430
You call that love?

351
00:30:16,349 --> 00:30:18,268
God will speak to you
in many tongues.

352
00:30:21,689 --> 00:30:24,650
If your heart is brave enough
to let him in.

353
00:31:31,174 --> 00:31:32,175
Stand aside!

354
00:31:32,593 --> 00:31:34,136
Let the abbess through.

355
00:31:39,432 --> 00:31:40,768
It hurts too much!

356
00:31:44,062 --> 00:31:45,355
It's torture!

357
00:31:45,648 --> 00:31:46,690
Hold her legs.

358
00:31:46,774 --> 00:31:47,733
Careful!

359
00:31:56,158 --> 00:31:57,117
Tie her down.

360
00:31:59,745 --> 00:32:00,954
Fetch the doctor.

361
00:32:18,305 --> 00:32:19,431
How is she?

362
00:32:19,515 --> 00:32:22,476
I gave her poppy juice to drink.
She's sleeping.

363
00:32:22,560 --> 00:32:23,644
What was it?

364
00:32:23,727 --> 00:32:25,479
I found nothing abnormal.

365
00:32:26,063 --> 00:32:27,856
But she is clearly in pain.

366
00:32:27,940 --> 00:32:29,942
She howled for hours on end.

367
00:32:30,818 --> 00:32:33,028
There's black bile in her urine.

368
00:32:33,111 --> 00:32:34,237
That's common.

369
00:32:35,614 --> 00:32:36,824
If it starts again?

370
00:32:37,407 --> 00:32:39,577
I'll leave you some poppy juice.

371
00:32:41,579 --> 00:32:42,621
20 dinari.

372
00:33:07,896 --> 00:33:09,397
Why are you so cruel?

373
00:33:19,658 --> 00:33:21,494
You want to be with me?

374
00:33:27,916 --> 00:33:29,627
I want to be with you.

375
00:34:52,585 --> 00:34:53,544
Jesus!

376
00:34:58,340 --> 00:35:00,050
Thank you, sweet Jesus!

377
00:35:03,887 --> 00:35:05,097
Benedetta,

378
00:35:05,639 --> 00:35:07,099
I shall heal your wound.

379
00:35:07,307 --> 00:35:08,809
You're not Jesus.

380
00:35:08,892 --> 00:35:10,060
I am Jesus.

381
00:35:11,061 --> 00:35:12,062
You are my bride.

382
00:35:12,521 --> 00:35:14,356
No! It's a lie!

383
00:35:17,275 --> 00:35:18,527
Give yourself to me!

384
00:35:22,698 --> 00:35:23,741
Bitch!

385
00:35:23,824 --> 00:35:25,325
I'll chop you to bits!

386
00:36:10,913 --> 00:36:12,873
You're getting a cellmate.

387
00:36:16,669 --> 00:36:17,711
Thanks.

388
00:36:31,266 --> 00:36:32,350
Feeling better?

389
00:36:33,226 --> 00:36:35,353
I feel what God wants me to feel.

390
00:36:35,854 --> 00:36:38,482
I've decided
to place someone at your side.

391
00:36:38,566 --> 00:36:40,484
To be with you day and night.

392
00:36:40,568 --> 00:36:43,403
To care for you, pray with you.

393
00:36:44,071 --> 00:36:46,239
Give you your remedy if necessary.

394
00:36:46,532 --> 00:36:48,534
I'm sorry to be such a burden.

395
00:36:48,617 --> 00:36:50,869
We'll see if this improves things.

396
00:36:57,000 --> 00:37:00,253
Bartolomea was the only sister
to volunteer for this duty.

397
00:37:00,713 --> 00:37:03,757
I hope there is something providential
in the choice.

398
00:37:04,967 --> 00:37:06,885
A lesson in forgiveness, perhaps.

399
00:37:13,684 --> 00:37:14,893
Why are you here?

400
00:37:16,979 --> 00:37:17,938
To torment me?

401
00:37:18,522 --> 00:37:21,108
Have I done something to suggest that?

402
00:37:34,622 --> 00:37:37,040
How can anyone put anything in here?

403
00:37:44,172 --> 00:37:46,800
The dress I wore the day I arrived here.

404
00:38:01,231 --> 00:38:02,190
And this?

405
00:38:06,028 --> 00:38:07,154
My mother's.

406
00:38:08,781 --> 00:38:10,323
A gift from her as a child.

407
00:38:12,743 --> 00:38:14,995
So let's put it...

408
00:38:15,078 --> 00:38:16,038
There!

409
00:38:30,761 --> 00:38:32,429
I was deceived by the devil.

410
00:38:33,221 --> 00:38:34,723
He made me hurt you.

411
00:38:35,933 --> 00:38:37,225
But you came back.

412
00:38:48,571 --> 00:38:49,905
You're out of bed?

413
00:38:50,614 --> 00:38:52,324
I want to be useful again.

414
00:38:52,825 --> 00:38:55,327
Reverend Mother
needed help with the accounts.

415
00:38:55,869 --> 00:38:56,954
What's all that?

416
00:38:58,664 --> 00:38:59,623
Numbers.

417
00:39:00,999 --> 00:39:02,042
Beyond me.

418
00:39:03,919 --> 00:39:04,878
I can teach you.

419
00:39:06,964 --> 00:39:08,966
I'm not very good at learning.

420
00:39:09,925 --> 00:39:10,926
Nice and warm.

421
00:39:11,635 --> 00:39:12,720
Anything else?

422
00:39:13,261 --> 00:39:14,304
No, thank you.

423
00:39:15,013 --> 00:39:16,223
I'm going to bed.

424
00:39:32,490 --> 00:39:34,116
I'm not allowed a look?

425
00:39:35,367 --> 00:39:37,160
We must not be seen nude.

426
00:39:38,454 --> 00:39:39,412
Really?

427
00:39:53,385 --> 00:39:54,344
Saw you!

428
00:39:57,097 --> 00:39:58,223
It was a joke.

429
00:39:59,266 --> 00:40:01,602
Only you find your jokes funny.

430
00:40:03,436 --> 00:40:04,480
Perhaps.

431
00:40:17,284 --> 00:40:18,619
I saw your breasts.

432
00:40:26,084 --> 00:40:27,044
I saw them.

433
00:40:47,690 --> 00:40:48,649
Benedetta...

434
00:41:03,205 --> 00:41:05,708
Will you suffer
to show your love for me?

435
00:41:09,545 --> 00:41:10,796
Take off your clothes.

436
00:41:12,506 --> 00:41:15,050
It's forbidden to be nude with others.

437
00:41:15,884 --> 00:41:16,885
Wherever I am,

438
00:41:17,344 --> 00:41:19,054
there can be no shame.

439
00:41:20,931 --> 00:41:21,932
Do as I say.

440
00:41:24,309 --> 00:41:25,268
Yes, Lord.

441
00:41:26,854 --> 00:41:27,813
I shall.

442
00:41:35,237 --> 00:41:36,238
Come to me.

443
00:41:53,464 --> 00:41:54,632
Remove what separates us.

444
00:42:06,644 --> 00:42:08,353
Place your hands on mine.

445
00:42:29,291 --> 00:42:30,584
Such pain!

446
00:42:30,668 --> 00:42:31,710
My God!

447
00:42:31,794 --> 00:42:33,378
My God, it hurts!

448
00:42:41,470 --> 00:42:42,596
Too much!

449
00:42:42,680 --> 00:42:43,764
I can't stand it.

450
00:42:56,944 --> 00:42:57,945
Help me.

451
00:42:58,278 --> 00:42:59,279
Help me!

452
00:43:34,106 --> 00:43:35,398
Jesus did this to me.

453
00:43:38,068 --> 00:43:39,444
Last night...

454
00:43:41,279 --> 00:43:42,364
He did this to me.

455
00:43:46,869 --> 00:43:47,828
Here, too.

456
00:43:49,497 --> 00:43:50,581
The stigmata!

457
00:44:11,184 --> 00:44:13,687
Were you praying when it happened?

458
00:44:14,688 --> 00:44:15,898
I was in bed.

459
00:44:15,981 --> 00:44:16,982
Asleep.

460
00:44:17,775 --> 00:44:19,234
That's when it happened.

461
00:44:19,818 --> 00:44:22,988
St. Francis was in prayer
when he received the stigmata.

462
00:44:23,947 --> 00:44:25,574
Catherine of Siena, also.

463
00:44:26,784 --> 00:44:28,452
Neither was sleeping.

464
00:44:29,119 --> 00:44:30,328
I was sleeping.

465
00:44:31,539 --> 00:44:32,748
And Jesus marked me.

466
00:44:32,831 --> 00:44:34,416
It was Jesus. I saw him.

467
00:44:35,709 --> 00:44:36,919
You saw him?

468
00:44:38,253 --> 00:44:39,713
I heard him speaking.

469
00:44:41,256 --> 00:44:42,340
What did he say?

470
00:44:44,760 --> 00:44:45,928
I don't remember.

471
00:44:48,096 --> 00:44:51,684
I'd expect the word of God
to make a greater impression.

472
00:44:52,726 --> 00:44:55,145
Bring Sister Benedetta to my chamber.

473
00:45:17,585 --> 00:45:18,711
Open it, will you?

474
00:45:25,968 --> 00:45:29,012
However often I wipe her wounds,
they bleed again.

475
00:45:29,096 --> 00:45:30,639
They are very deep.

476
00:45:31,974 --> 00:45:32,975
Look.

477
00:45:42,317 --> 00:45:43,652
Her feet are the same.

478
00:45:44,319 --> 00:45:45,488
And her side?

479
00:45:45,571 --> 00:45:46,530
Worse.

480
00:45:47,656 --> 00:45:49,199
How is this possible?

481
00:45:49,282 --> 00:45:51,994
I don't know.
I've never seen the like.

482
00:45:52,077 --> 00:45:53,454
What can we do?

483
00:45:53,829 --> 00:45:55,038
Keep them clean.

484
00:45:55,413 --> 00:45:57,374
New dressings every two hours.

485
00:45:58,626 --> 00:46:00,043
Remove her wimple.

486
00:46:09,637 --> 00:46:10,638
No blood.

487
00:46:12,430 --> 00:46:13,474
It hurts.

488
00:46:15,601 --> 00:46:18,771
When he was made to wear
the crown of thorns,

489
00:46:18,854 --> 00:46:20,689
Jesus's forehead bled.

490
00:46:22,733 --> 00:46:23,942
I don't see anything.

491
00:46:24,818 --> 00:46:25,944
Dress her wounds.

492
00:46:26,612 --> 00:46:27,613
Close after us.

493
00:46:32,367 --> 00:46:33,661
You are doubtful?

494
00:46:34,662 --> 00:46:35,996
The girl was in bed.

495
00:46:36,747 --> 00:46:39,583
No miracle occurs in bed, believe me.

496
00:46:39,667 --> 00:46:41,084
What do I write?

497
00:46:44,421 --> 00:46:47,090
The absence of signs on her head
is troubling.

498
00:46:48,634 --> 00:46:50,844
In all confirmed cases of stigmata,

499
00:46:50,928 --> 00:46:54,014
evidence of the crown of thorns
was recorded.

500
00:46:54,473 --> 00:46:56,725
God is not bound by any rule book.

501
00:46:58,894 --> 00:47:00,020
Do we agree?

502
00:47:01,564 --> 00:47:03,691
- Your Grace?
- Yes, my child.

503
00:47:03,774 --> 00:47:04,900
May I go?

504
00:47:05,484 --> 00:47:06,485
Of course.

505
00:47:12,032 --> 00:47:14,076
Would you care for a glass of wine?

506
00:47:14,409 --> 00:47:15,453
Most gladly.

507
00:47:18,456 --> 00:47:20,541
Leave me. I need to pray.

508
00:47:31,134 --> 00:47:33,679
You find me too willing
to believe this miracle?

509
00:47:33,762 --> 00:47:36,807
My dear provost,
I don't think you believe it at all.

510
00:47:38,266 --> 00:47:39,602
Am I so cynical?

511
00:47:40,478 --> 00:47:41,436
Perhaps.

512
00:47:42,062 --> 00:47:44,022
Unless I have a vision of my own.

513
00:47:45,566 --> 00:47:46,692
It seems possible.

514
00:47:48,235 --> 00:47:50,488
A vision of St. Francis, perhaps?

515
00:47:51,572 --> 00:47:54,533
Assisi was once an insignificant village.

516
00:47:54,617 --> 00:47:56,326
Now, pilgrims flood there.

517
00:47:57,369 --> 00:47:59,246
Filling both its basilicas.

518
00:47:59,788 --> 00:48:02,415
Administered by a bishop,
not a provost.

519
00:48:05,836 --> 00:48:07,713
Jesus, what's happening to me?

520
00:48:20,225 --> 00:48:21,519
<i>Blasphemy!</i>

521
00:48:22,019 --> 00:48:24,229
<i>Know, O sinners,</i>

522
00:48:24,688 --> 00:48:27,399
<i>that as plague stalks the land,</i>

523
00:48:27,483 --> 00:48:30,778
<i>Pescia has been spared
only by the grace</i>

524
00:48:30,861 --> 00:48:32,112
<i>of my bride!</i>

525
00:48:33,030 --> 00:48:34,364
<i>You harass,</i>

526
00:48:34,447 --> 00:48:36,534
<i>torment and persecute</i>

527
00:48:36,617 --> 00:48:38,702
<i>she who has protected you!</i>

528
00:48:48,629 --> 00:48:49,838
What did you see?

529
00:48:49,922 --> 00:48:51,048
She fell.

530
00:48:55,594 --> 00:48:57,012
A timely miracle.

531
00:48:59,014 --> 00:49:01,892
Your Grace, this has gone far enough.

532
00:49:02,225 --> 00:49:04,687
You'd bring the fury of God upon us?

533
00:49:05,521 --> 00:49:07,856
You heard the words spoken
a moment ago.

534
00:49:07,940 --> 00:49:10,734
- I heard words.
- You mock me now as well?

535
00:49:14,404 --> 00:49:17,700
The child's words,
however troubling, are of God.

536
00:49:18,283 --> 00:49:20,410
I feel it deep in my soul.

537
00:49:20,494 --> 00:49:24,289
This miracle glorifies the Theatines.
Can you not see?

538
00:49:26,667 --> 00:49:27,751
I see, your Grace.

539
00:49:29,962 --> 00:49:30,963
You act docile...

540
00:49:33,006 --> 00:49:35,634
but you'll stab me
as soon as I turn my back.

541
00:49:36,301 --> 00:49:37,260
Well,

542
00:49:37,678 --> 00:49:40,681
we'll see if God gives us all we desire.

543
00:49:46,186 --> 00:49:47,646
Praise be to Benedetta.

544
00:49:49,648 --> 00:49:50,899
Santa Benedetta.

545
00:49:51,399 --> 00:49:53,443
Bless us all, Santa Benedetta.

546
00:49:56,864 --> 00:49:59,533
People really will think
Benedetta's a saint,

547
00:49:59,617 --> 00:50:01,619
when we know it's nonsense.

548
00:50:03,787 --> 00:50:04,747
Do we?

549
00:50:04,997 --> 00:50:07,625
You remark on her unwounded brow,

550
00:50:07,875 --> 00:50:11,128
and suddenly, she smashes a glass
and wounds appear.

551
00:50:11,211 --> 00:50:13,046
Did you see her?
Were you there?

552
00:50:15,716 --> 00:50:16,717
No.

553
00:50:16,800 --> 00:50:18,176
So you know nothing.

554
00:50:24,307 --> 00:50:25,350
I saw nothing.

555
00:50:26,268 --> 00:50:27,269
But I know.

556
00:50:27,352 --> 00:50:28,687
How do you know?

557
00:50:29,146 --> 00:50:30,313
Did God show you?

558
00:50:31,148 --> 00:50:32,941
Did you have a vision also?

559
00:50:45,287 --> 00:50:46,830
Why are you defending her?

560
00:50:52,670 --> 00:50:55,422
We don't always understand
the instruments God uses.

561
00:50:55,839 --> 00:50:59,009
Perhaps he put Benedetta in a trance
and in that state,

562
00:50:59,384 --> 00:51:00,636
she harmed herself.

563
00:51:02,345 --> 00:51:04,682
Or perhaps God sent us a madwoman,

564
00:51:06,517 --> 00:51:09,478
who spouts nonsense to serve his ends.

565
00:51:18,236 --> 00:51:20,322
<i>I want you to give me your heart.</i>

566
00:51:21,782 --> 00:51:24,201
<i>Will I not die without my heart?</i>

567
00:51:24,952 --> 00:51:27,287
<i>You will live. Do you love me?</i>

568
00:51:28,622 --> 00:51:30,749
<i>Can I love you without a heart?</i>

569
00:51:30,833 --> 00:51:32,501
<i>I'll give you a new one.</i>

570
00:51:33,210 --> 00:51:34,169
<i>Mine.</i>

571
00:51:39,717 --> 00:51:40,801
Bartolomea...

572
00:51:43,762 --> 00:51:44,763
What?

573
00:51:44,847 --> 00:51:46,724
Jesus gave me a new heart.

574
00:51:47,933 --> 00:51:49,184
It's so big!

575
00:51:50,393 --> 00:51:52,062
Too big for my chest.

576
00:51:53,606 --> 00:51:54,648
Feel it.

577
00:51:56,525 --> 00:51:57,943
Feel how big it is!

578
00:52:16,879 --> 00:52:17,838
Yes.

579
00:52:18,171 --> 00:52:19,465
I feel it.

580
00:52:25,888 --> 00:52:26,930
What's wrong?

581
00:52:27,014 --> 00:52:29,057
Benedetta had a nightmare.

582
00:52:29,141 --> 00:52:30,225
I'm fine.

583
00:52:32,144 --> 00:52:33,145
Goodnight.

584
00:52:35,313 --> 00:52:36,565
Go to your beds.

585
00:53:34,122 --> 00:53:36,249
Something wonderful has happened to us.

586
00:53:37,375 --> 00:53:41,171
Jesus Christ
has chosen our blessed sister,

587
00:53:41,547 --> 00:53:42,590
Benedetta.

588
00:53:44,299 --> 00:53:45,718
We saw her wounds.

589
00:53:46,927 --> 00:53:48,596
The wounds of Jesus!

590
00:53:48,929 --> 00:53:50,263
Praise the Lord!

591
00:53:52,683 --> 00:53:53,726
Jesus chose her.

592
00:53:55,143 --> 00:53:56,436
That is why we,

593
00:53:56,687 --> 00:53:59,231
invested with the powers of his Church,

594
00:53:59,648 --> 00:54:02,442
choose Benedetta to be abbess

595
00:54:02,651 --> 00:54:04,444
of the Convent of the Theatines.

596
00:54:04,528 --> 00:54:06,154
<i>In nomine Patris</i>

597
00:54:06,238 --> 00:54:09,074
<i>et Filii et Spiritus Sancti...</i>

598
00:54:09,533 --> 00:54:10,493
Amen!

599
00:54:11,368 --> 00:54:12,369
<i>Oremus!</i>

600
00:54:12,870 --> 00:54:13,912
Lord God...

601
00:54:19,752 --> 00:54:20,878
This cannot be.

602
00:54:21,419 --> 00:54:22,546
Sister Christina,

603
00:54:23,171 --> 00:54:24,548
what has come over you?

604
00:54:28,969 --> 00:54:30,929
With all due respect, Father...

605
00:54:32,430 --> 00:54:33,557
it is for us...

606
00:54:34,808 --> 00:54:37,144
Us! As sisters of this convent...

607
00:54:37,978 --> 00:54:39,437
to choose a new abbess.

608
00:54:40,272 --> 00:54:41,690
And only us!

609
00:54:41,774 --> 00:54:43,066
Jesus has chosen.

610
00:54:43,441 --> 00:54:44,652
Your Lord and Master.

611
00:54:45,486 --> 00:54:46,487
It is God's will.

612
00:54:47,070 --> 00:54:50,157
But who decides what is God's will?

613
00:54:50,240 --> 00:54:51,909
Don't we, as sisters...

614
00:54:51,992 --> 00:54:53,035
Christina!

615
00:54:53,702 --> 00:54:54,745
Withdraw.

616
00:54:58,916 --> 00:54:59,875
Now.

617
00:55:12,095 --> 00:55:13,556
<i>Causa finita.</i>

618
00:55:14,557 --> 00:55:17,225
I ask the Reverend Mother

619
00:55:17,309 --> 00:55:18,936
to relinquish her functions.

620
00:55:34,827 --> 00:55:35,828
Sister Benedetta!

621
00:55:37,079 --> 00:55:38,038
Come forward.

622
00:56:43,228 --> 00:56:44,187
It's bouncy.

623
00:56:44,813 --> 00:56:46,231
- It's my bed.
- So soft.

624
00:56:52,237 --> 00:56:53,614
And it's all ours.

625
00:57:04,625 --> 00:57:05,918
Sister Jacopa fell!

626
00:57:06,251 --> 00:57:07,503
She can't move!

627
00:57:20,849 --> 00:57:22,350
I doubt she'll last the day.

628
00:57:24,436 --> 00:57:25,479
Reverend Mother,

629
00:57:25,896 --> 00:57:27,147
I'll stay with her.

630
00:57:27,481 --> 00:57:28,440
Of course.

631
00:57:29,316 --> 00:57:32,736
But if she doesn't go by vespers,
you must leave her side.

632
00:57:32,820 --> 00:57:35,614
It will be my first divine office
as abbess.

633
00:57:36,448 --> 00:57:38,325
Jesus told me you must attend.

634
00:57:39,910 --> 00:57:41,203
Yes, Reverend Mother.

635
00:57:42,538 --> 00:57:44,414
I'll stay with Sister Jacopa.

636
00:57:44,498 --> 00:57:45,874
Until lauds, if necessary.

637
00:57:46,291 --> 00:57:47,250
Perfect.

638
00:57:48,043 --> 00:57:49,503
Jesus didn't mention you.

639
00:57:59,930 --> 00:58:02,933
They throw mud in your face
and you say nothing.

640
00:58:03,016 --> 00:58:04,685
It's how the game is played.

641
00:58:04,977 --> 00:58:07,145
And in the end, we all win.

642
00:58:07,521 --> 00:58:11,149
The provost gets his bishopric
and the Theatines will prosper.

643
00:58:11,525 --> 00:58:12,610
That's so important?

644
00:58:14,111 --> 00:58:17,948
It may be vain and useless
but I have devoted my life to it.

645
00:58:22,536 --> 00:58:25,539
I had one life to give
and I chose this convent.

646
00:58:26,331 --> 00:58:27,791
Perhaps it chose me.

647
00:58:30,127 --> 00:58:31,294
Mother, you can't...

648
00:58:31,378 --> 00:58:33,213
Call me Sister Felicita.

649
00:58:34,673 --> 00:58:38,010
People have to know.
What's going on here is blasphemy.

650
00:58:38,093 --> 00:58:40,262
Everyone who matters already knows.

651
00:58:40,763 --> 00:58:42,681
If they don't denounce Benedetta,

652
00:58:42,765 --> 00:58:45,225
they don't want her to be denounced.

653
00:58:46,268 --> 00:58:48,604
If you speak out, they'll destroy you.

654
00:58:49,062 --> 00:58:50,230
You'll be alone.

655
00:58:52,149 --> 00:58:53,484
I will not defend you.

656
00:58:56,737 --> 00:58:59,197
Time for vespers, Sister Felicita.

657
00:59:42,491 --> 00:59:43,576
Lies.

658
01:00:26,535 --> 01:00:27,495
Father...

659
01:00:28,746 --> 01:00:29,913
I want to confess.

660
01:00:29,997 --> 01:00:31,206
At this hour?

661
01:00:31,289 --> 01:00:32,916
I must, Father. Please.

662
01:00:34,209 --> 01:00:37,254
You refused to bow before God.
Have you repented?

663
01:00:38,005 --> 01:00:40,048
The Lord taught me never to lie.

664
01:00:41,008 --> 01:00:42,968
And that has led me to repentance.

665
01:01:04,740 --> 01:01:05,741
Speak.

666
01:01:05,824 --> 01:01:09,327
Restore your bonds to the Lord,
the living Christ.

667
01:01:12,122 --> 01:01:14,917
It concerns Sister Benedetta. I...

668
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:16,502
You refer to the Reverend Mother?

669
01:01:19,296 --> 01:01:20,255
Yes.

670
01:01:21,298 --> 01:01:23,258
Yes, I refer to the Reverend Mother.

671
01:01:24,259 --> 01:01:26,136
She's a false prophetess.

672
01:01:26,219 --> 01:01:28,764
Her miracle was false.
She created her stigmata.

673
01:01:28,847 --> 01:01:31,559
This is confession.
You came to accuse others?

674
01:01:32,893 --> 01:01:35,270
I accuse myself of remaining silent.

675
01:01:36,021 --> 01:01:37,022
It was cowardice.

676
01:01:41,443 --> 01:01:42,778
Do you have proof?

677
01:01:43,195 --> 01:01:45,363
The stigmata on her head.

678
01:01:46,574 --> 01:01:48,366
She used a shard of glass

679
01:01:48,867 --> 01:01:51,369
to lacerate her brow and make it bleed.

680
01:01:53,872 --> 01:01:55,248
Did you witness this?

681
01:02:00,879 --> 01:02:01,839
Yes.

682
01:02:13,016 --> 01:02:14,017
A three!

683
01:02:15,185 --> 01:02:16,186
That is a...

684
01:02:17,646 --> 01:02:19,690
- Four.
- Yes, go on.

685
01:02:23,986 --> 01:02:25,738
You're pressing too hard.

686
01:02:29,241 --> 01:02:30,367
Try again.

687
01:02:32,453 --> 01:02:34,121
- I can't.
- You can.

688
01:02:37,082 --> 01:02:38,041
Come on.

689
01:03:47,069 --> 01:03:48,070
Come.

690
01:03:52,741 --> 01:03:53,784
Come.

691
01:04:59,266 --> 01:05:00,601
You want to see them?

692
01:05:01,935 --> 01:05:02,895
Show me.

693
01:05:55,906 --> 01:05:56,865
Go deeper.

694
01:05:57,491 --> 01:05:58,451
Deeper!

695
01:05:59,535 --> 01:06:00,494
I can't.

696
01:06:01,454 --> 01:06:02,663
My hand's too big.

697
01:06:05,958 --> 01:06:06,917
Want a taste?

698
01:06:33,902 --> 01:06:34,903
My God...

699
01:06:43,954 --> 01:06:44,913
No!

700
01:06:48,751 --> 01:06:49,710
Yes!

701
01:06:50,335 --> 01:06:51,462
Yes, come now!

702
01:06:53,421 --> 01:06:54,381
Come!

703
01:07:00,638 --> 01:07:01,680
It won't stop!

704
01:07:08,646 --> 01:07:09,855
My sweet Jesus!

705
01:07:28,707 --> 01:07:29,833
You want more?

706
01:08:28,140 --> 01:08:31,687
Today's reading is taken from Leviticus.

707
01:08:33,313 --> 01:08:35,147
But before I begin,

708
01:08:35,566 --> 01:08:39,361
I want to address questions
troubling the hearts of some sisters.

709
01:08:40,821 --> 01:08:41,779
Sister Christina.

710
01:08:43,030 --> 01:08:44,700
If something preys on your mind,

711
01:08:46,368 --> 01:08:48,285
it is your duty to express it.

712
01:08:50,205 --> 01:08:52,332
You want me to talk now?

713
01:08:53,375 --> 01:08:55,085
- Here?
- Where else?

714
01:08:56,253 --> 01:08:58,796
Pour out your heart. Stand, speak.

715
01:09:08,098 --> 01:09:09,349
Go ahead, speak!

716
01:09:19,692 --> 01:09:20,986
Our Mother Superior

717
01:09:22,194 --> 01:09:23,155
deceives us,

718
01:09:24,031 --> 01:09:24,990
lies to us.

719
01:09:26,033 --> 01:09:27,449
Sister, explain yourself.

720
01:09:28,410 --> 01:09:31,454
Do you have a grievance
against our Reverend Mother?

721
01:09:33,330 --> 01:09:34,457
All I know is...

722
01:09:36,208 --> 01:09:37,252
What do you know?

723
01:09:44,802 --> 01:09:46,053
Benedetta tricks us.

724
01:09:47,596 --> 01:09:49,264
She marked her forehead herself.

725
01:09:50,265 --> 01:09:51,308
When she fell,

726
01:09:51,559 --> 01:09:53,101
she broke a glass jar and...

727
01:09:53,185 --> 01:09:54,394
cut herself with it.

728
01:09:54,853 --> 01:09:55,813
I saw her.

729
01:09:56,063 --> 01:09:58,148
My dear sister, what are you saying?

730
01:09:58,356 --> 01:10:00,192
And I'm sure the other signs

731
01:10:00,275 --> 01:10:01,860
came about the same way.

732
01:10:03,278 --> 01:10:04,404
Sister Christina...

733
01:10:05,739 --> 01:10:06,740
So you saw

734
01:10:07,240 --> 01:10:10,494
our Reverend Mother cut herself
with a shard of glass?

735
01:10:10,578 --> 01:10:11,704
Is that right?

736
01:10:12,079 --> 01:10:14,372
Yes. And I told the abbess.

737
01:10:22,089 --> 01:10:23,466
What did you tell her?

738
01:10:24,508 --> 01:10:25,634
What I saw.

739
01:10:26,802 --> 01:10:28,721
What Sister Benedetta did.

740
01:10:31,557 --> 01:10:32,766
You do know

741
01:10:33,391 --> 01:10:35,268
false witness is a mortal sin?

742
01:10:37,980 --> 01:10:39,773
I'm not the one who lies.

743
01:10:44,528 --> 01:10:45,488
Sister Felicita,

744
01:10:46,655 --> 01:10:47,781
step forward.

745
01:11:03,547 --> 01:11:04,840
Did Sister Christina

746
01:11:05,340 --> 01:11:08,469
tell you that she saw Sister Benedetta

747
01:11:08,552 --> 01:11:11,221
inflicting wounds on her own forehead?

748
01:11:13,306 --> 01:11:14,933
She had serious doubts.

749
01:11:15,851 --> 01:11:17,019
But did she see it?

750
01:11:19,312 --> 01:11:21,899
She did not say
she witnessed it directly...

751
01:11:21,982 --> 01:11:23,358
Directly?

752
01:11:23,441 --> 01:11:25,027
Did she witness it or not?

753
01:11:29,281 --> 01:11:30,240
No.

754
01:11:34,161 --> 01:11:35,454
She did not witness it.

755
01:11:41,710 --> 01:11:42,878
Liar!

756
01:11:43,921 --> 01:11:45,255
<i>She denies me!</i>

757
01:11:45,631 --> 01:11:47,049
<i>Satan has possessed her!</i>

758
01:11:47,925 --> 01:11:48,884
<i>Punish her!</i>

759
01:11:49,968 --> 01:11:51,219
<i>Flagellation!</i>

760
01:11:51,679 --> 01:11:53,305
<i>She must flagellate herself!</i>

761
01:11:53,388 --> 01:11:55,933
The devil must be driven out of your body!

762
01:11:58,268 --> 01:11:59,436
Bare yourself!

763
01:12:14,868 --> 01:12:16,495
Free yourself of the demon.

764
01:12:16,912 --> 01:12:18,539
Strike, my dear sister!

765
01:12:56,076 --> 01:12:57,035
At last!

766
01:13:00,122 --> 01:13:01,414
The rain has stopped.

767
01:13:02,458 --> 01:13:03,792
I have a gift for you.

768
01:13:19,975 --> 01:13:22,645
It will go deeper than my fingers.
Want to try?

769
01:13:26,273 --> 01:13:27,733
It's a little rough here.

770
01:13:29,985 --> 01:13:31,069
Yes.

771
01:13:31,153 --> 01:13:32,362
I'll see to it.

772
01:13:33,363 --> 01:13:34,406
Take this off.

773
01:13:43,832 --> 01:13:45,543
You enjoyed it, didn't you?

774
01:13:46,084 --> 01:13:47,377
What did I enjoy?

775
01:13:48,170 --> 01:13:50,172
Christina whipping herself.
I saw you.

776
01:13:51,298 --> 01:13:52,466
No, you're wrong.

777
01:13:53,759 --> 01:13:54,760
It was later.

778
01:13:58,847 --> 01:14:00,140
Thinking of you.

779
01:14:01,058 --> 01:14:02,601
Of what it would be like.

780
01:14:12,069 --> 01:14:13,529
Shall we try?

781
01:14:25,583 --> 01:14:26,667
Nice and smooth.

782
01:14:34,424 --> 01:14:35,425
It hurts?

783
01:14:37,094 --> 01:14:38,303
No, it feels good.

784
01:15:15,758 --> 01:15:16,925
There's a fire?

785
01:15:31,231 --> 01:15:32,440
Is it a star?

786
01:15:32,775 --> 01:15:33,776
A comet.

787
01:16:07,225 --> 01:16:09,603
The comet is directly over our convent.

788
01:16:10,145 --> 01:16:13,315
- What does it mean?
- It's a sign from God. A warning.

789
01:16:13,398 --> 01:16:15,233
Something terrible will happen.

790
01:17:32,394 --> 01:17:33,604
What have you done?

791
01:17:35,648 --> 01:17:37,024
What have you done?

792
01:17:37,107 --> 01:17:39,860
You silly girl, what have you done?

793
01:17:43,405 --> 01:17:44,990
I'll lay hands on her

794
01:17:45,073 --> 01:17:47,117
to intercede for her soul.

795
01:17:47,200 --> 01:17:48,201
Intercede?

796
01:17:48,285 --> 01:17:49,578
Don't touch her!

797
01:17:50,621 --> 01:17:51,580
I must!

798
01:17:52,330 --> 01:17:54,542
A suicide's soul is bound for hell.

799
01:17:54,625 --> 01:17:55,626
I can intervene.

800
01:17:56,001 --> 01:17:57,878
Hands off her! Get away!

801
01:17:58,420 --> 01:18:01,256
A word from me
and Jesus saves her from the flames.

802
01:18:02,675 --> 01:18:04,384
You're the one who'll...

803
01:18:08,221 --> 01:18:09,222
Stop!

804
01:18:13,143 --> 01:18:14,978
You lying bitch!

805
01:18:15,062 --> 01:18:16,104
Whore!

806
01:19:18,333 --> 01:19:19,752
She gave me an order.

807
01:19:20,418 --> 01:19:22,546
Even if she's not abbess...

808
01:19:22,630 --> 01:19:23,839
Where did she go?

809
01:19:26,133 --> 01:19:27,175
To Florence.

810
01:19:34,808 --> 01:19:36,434
Sister Felicita has left.

811
01:19:36,977 --> 01:19:38,479
Going to Florence.

812
01:19:39,396 --> 01:19:40,355
Why?

813
01:19:43,316 --> 01:19:45,193
To see the Nuncio, I suppose.

814
01:19:48,906 --> 01:19:50,032
And tell him what?

815
01:19:54,578 --> 01:19:56,413
What do you fear she'll tell him?

816
01:19:58,832 --> 01:19:59,833
Everything.

817
01:20:01,919 --> 01:20:02,961
Meaning?

818
01:20:05,422 --> 01:20:07,090
That my miracles aren't real?

819
01:20:08,717 --> 01:20:10,177
No, I didn't mean that.

820
01:20:13,847 --> 01:20:14,807
That...

821
01:20:16,642 --> 01:20:18,852
I cut myself with a stupid shard.

822
01:20:21,522 --> 01:20:23,398
That's what you did, isn't it?

823
01:20:25,484 --> 01:20:26,485
Didn't you?

824
01:20:27,986 --> 01:20:28,946
I don't know.

825
01:20:30,864 --> 01:20:33,158
I don't know
how God makes things happen.

826
01:20:34,117 --> 01:20:35,994
But his will is done through me.

827
01:20:40,123 --> 01:20:41,667
This is not my flesh alone.

828
01:20:44,712 --> 01:20:46,046
It is his also.

829
01:20:48,423 --> 01:20:50,551
Stop! You disgust me.

830
01:20:58,308 --> 01:20:59,643
That's what you fear.

831
01:21:02,145 --> 01:21:04,607
What Sister Felicita might say about us.

832
01:21:05,107 --> 01:21:06,274
And what we do.

833
01:21:13,949 --> 01:21:15,451
Should we be ashamed?

834
01:21:19,287 --> 01:21:22,958
Shame does not exist
under the protection of God's love.

835
01:21:25,210 --> 01:21:26,336
God's love?

836
01:21:27,588 --> 01:21:28,714
You love only yourself.

837
01:21:34,261 --> 01:21:36,221
- So come closer.
- No.

838
01:21:43,395 --> 01:21:44,605
Just your breasts.

839
01:21:47,566 --> 01:21:48,567
Please.

840
01:22:13,676 --> 01:22:14,718
My Jesus, no!

841
01:22:16,136 --> 01:22:17,930
Don't ask that of me, please!

842
01:22:18,889 --> 01:22:19,932
Benedetta?

843
01:22:37,825 --> 01:22:39,868
The sisters must dig a grave.

844
01:23:42,430 --> 01:23:43,390
Where's Teresa?

845
01:23:44,224 --> 01:23:47,352
At the hospital.
She won't survive, your Excellency.

846
01:23:47,853 --> 01:23:49,187
Probably not, no.

847
01:23:50,313 --> 01:23:52,149
That's three since Sunday

848
01:23:52,232 --> 01:23:53,609
but I'm not afraid.

849
01:23:55,402 --> 01:23:57,905
Perhaps because
you're too full of life.

850
01:23:58,989 --> 01:24:01,158
A few more weeks and he'll be here.

851
01:24:01,241 --> 01:24:02,535
I already have milk.

852
01:24:07,540 --> 01:24:08,499
Enough.

853
01:24:16,339 --> 01:24:18,842
Is there anything you'd like to add?

854
01:24:18,926 --> 01:24:20,302
I told you everything.

855
01:24:20,385 --> 01:24:21,970
It's in your hands now.

856
01:24:25,140 --> 01:24:29,227
Extraordinary accusations
require extraordinary proof.

857
01:24:29,311 --> 01:24:30,688
I spoke only the truth.

858
01:24:31,564 --> 01:24:33,774
You may suspect my motives,

859
01:24:33,857 --> 01:24:35,275
but come to Pescia

860
01:24:35,734 --> 01:24:37,486
and you'll see for yourself.

861
01:24:41,114 --> 01:24:42,741
If you look honestly.

862
01:24:50,415 --> 01:24:53,251
If there is devilry in Pescia,
I shall unmask it.

863
01:24:53,335 --> 01:24:56,296
And if this sister is guilty of blasphemy,

864
01:24:56,379 --> 01:24:57,465
she will burn.

865
01:24:58,423 --> 01:25:01,093
But if your testimony proves false...

866
01:25:03,053 --> 01:25:04,597
what shall we do with you?

867
01:25:05,514 --> 01:25:06,682
Who can say?

868
01:25:09,560 --> 01:25:10,519
Yes...

869
01:25:13,271 --> 01:25:14,231
Me.

870
01:25:24,074 --> 01:25:25,451
Our Lord!

871
01:25:26,869 --> 01:25:27,870
Jesus!

872
01:25:43,385 --> 01:25:44,678
Kyrie!

873
01:25:49,725 --> 01:25:50,851
Jesus!

874
01:25:52,144 --> 01:25:53,687
Have mercy on us!

875
01:26:19,296 --> 01:26:21,674
It is a sign of God's judgment!

876
01:26:22,257 --> 01:26:24,677
"For the 3rd angel sounded his trumpet

877
01:26:24,760 --> 01:26:28,096
"and a great star fell from the sky
like a torch.

878
01:26:28,514 --> 01:26:31,475
"Its pestilence will poison
a third of the waters."

879
01:26:31,559 --> 01:26:32,518
The plague!

880
01:26:33,018 --> 01:26:34,603
The instrument to punish us.

881
01:26:35,437 --> 01:26:37,815
The plague will come to Pescia!

882
01:27:20,357 --> 01:27:21,525
Thank you, Lord.

883
01:27:23,318 --> 01:27:24,361
Thank you!

884
01:27:29,742 --> 01:27:30,826
Do not fear.

885
01:27:32,119 --> 01:27:35,122
The comet is the sign
that the Lord protects us.

886
01:27:36,081 --> 01:27:38,208
The plague will not touch Pescia!

887
01:27:40,335 --> 01:27:43,130
Jesus made a promise to me, his bride,

888
01:27:43,213 --> 01:27:44,965
to spare this town!

889
01:27:45,048 --> 01:27:46,884
Lord Jesus, protect us!

890
01:27:47,259 --> 01:27:48,886
Protect our city!

891
01:27:51,472 --> 01:27:53,056
Thank you, Lord Jesus!

892
01:27:57,102 --> 01:27:58,145
My sweet Jesus,

893
01:27:58,896 --> 01:28:00,814
we know you are among us.

894
01:28:01,524 --> 01:28:02,900
Thank you, my God.

895
01:28:12,325 --> 01:28:13,869
Shut the city gates!

896
01:28:14,202 --> 01:28:15,746
Let no one enter.

897
01:28:18,916 --> 01:28:20,584
It is the will of the Lord.

898
01:28:21,168 --> 01:28:22,419
Shut the gates now!

899
01:28:42,355 --> 01:28:43,315
Sister?

900
01:28:45,568 --> 01:28:46,527
What is happening?

901
01:28:57,955 --> 01:28:59,457
The grave is for you?

902
01:29:02,375 --> 01:29:03,376
Answer me.

903
01:29:37,995 --> 01:29:39,997
A letter! It came from heaven!

904
01:29:40,080 --> 01:29:41,499
The end is nigh!

905
01:29:43,125 --> 01:29:44,543
Let the bell toll!

906
01:29:46,128 --> 01:29:48,005
It is written! Read it!

907
01:29:48,088 --> 01:29:49,548
It's a letter from God!

908
01:30:01,519 --> 01:30:02,645
Nuncio!

909
01:30:02,728 --> 01:30:04,021
Give me absolution.

910
01:30:04,480 --> 01:30:06,314
Your Excellency, I'm dying.

911
01:30:06,815 --> 01:30:08,358
Do not let me die like this.

912
01:30:08,441 --> 01:30:10,068
Seek out your parish priest.

913
01:30:10,152 --> 01:30:11,654
Ask him for absolution.

914
01:30:12,237 --> 01:30:13,363
That's me.

915
01:30:13,446 --> 01:30:15,282
I'm the parish priest!

916
01:30:37,054 --> 01:30:38,764
Open the gates for the nuncio!

917
01:30:39,848 --> 01:30:41,141
The gates stay shut.

918
01:30:41,892 --> 01:30:43,561
No one in, no one out.

919
01:30:44,895 --> 01:30:47,314
I'm the nuncio of Florence. Open up!

920
01:30:47,397 --> 01:30:50,108
Even if you're the pope,
we won't open up.

921
01:30:50,192 --> 01:30:52,653
You're under my authority,
the Church's authority.

922
01:30:53,361 --> 01:30:55,989
Here we're under the authority
of Jesus himself.

923
01:30:56,073 --> 01:30:57,616
The gates stay shut!

924
01:31:05,583 --> 01:31:06,834
Your Excellency.

925
01:31:08,085 --> 01:31:09,587
I am the provost of Pescia.

926
01:31:11,338 --> 01:31:13,632
I am Alfonso Giglioli, papal nuncio,

927
01:31:13,716 --> 01:31:15,884
here to talk
to the abbess of the Theatines.

928
01:31:17,010 --> 01:31:19,054
It grieves me to tell you,

929
01:31:19,137 --> 01:31:21,890
the holy Benedetta died this afternoon.

930
01:31:24,602 --> 01:31:26,937
We are sorry you came all this way.

931
01:31:27,563 --> 01:31:30,733
I'll celebrate the funeral mass with you.
Take me to her.

932
01:31:30,816 --> 01:31:31,859
Let's go.

933
01:31:34,361 --> 01:31:36,113
The plague must stay outside.

934
01:31:37,364 --> 01:31:40,743
Anyone who enters must be examined
by our doctors.

935
01:31:40,826 --> 01:31:41,910
Even you, Excellency.

936
01:31:41,994 --> 01:31:43,621
God has sent us.

937
01:31:43,704 --> 01:31:45,623
And you will not stop us.

938
01:31:46,665 --> 01:31:47,708
We go in.

939
01:32:13,692 --> 01:32:14,777
Open up.

940
01:32:19,239 --> 01:32:21,408
An honor to welcome you, Excellency.

941
01:32:37,758 --> 01:32:39,968
You chose today to put on a theatrical?

942
01:32:40,052 --> 01:32:41,344
No, your Excellency.

943
01:32:41,428 --> 01:32:44,598
Before she died, the abbess revealed
how God wanted us

944
01:32:44,682 --> 01:32:46,809
to celebrate her ascension to heaven.

945
01:32:46,892 --> 01:32:50,187
- Another vision?
- Yes, Excellency, exactly.

946
01:32:50,270 --> 01:32:54,650
Her coffin was to be carried
by nine novices dressed as angels.

947
01:33:19,842 --> 01:33:21,218
Skin intact.

948
01:33:21,802 --> 01:33:22,886
No trace of plague.

949
01:33:23,971 --> 01:33:25,556
She received the last rites?

950
01:33:25,639 --> 01:33:27,891
No, her death was too sudden.

951
01:33:28,476 --> 01:33:30,185
I shall administer them now.

952
01:33:30,644 --> 01:33:32,020
Make preparations.

953
01:33:32,771 --> 01:33:33,981
Are you satisfied?

954
01:33:35,440 --> 01:33:37,526
I never wanted her to die.

955
01:33:39,236 --> 01:33:40,821
Not so quickly, at least.

956
01:34:08,015 --> 01:34:09,475
Jesus, hold onto me!

957
01:34:10,809 --> 01:34:12,269
Don't let me go back!

958
01:34:13,646 --> 01:34:15,564
I want to stay with you.

959
01:34:26,825 --> 01:34:29,369
I was in heaven, in perfect peace.

960
01:34:29,828 --> 01:34:31,497
But I was torn from it.

961
01:34:32,205 --> 01:34:35,125
Like a baby from the womb,
I was sent back.

962
01:34:37,169 --> 01:34:39,379
Jesus brought me back here to Earth.

963
01:34:39,463 --> 01:34:40,756
Why so, mother?

964
01:34:43,509 --> 01:34:46,178
I saw the souls
of those who are soon to die.

965
01:34:48,972 --> 01:34:51,600
I saw your souls, shed floods of tears.

966
01:34:54,311 --> 01:34:56,855
You saw mine as well, I suppose?

967
01:34:57,815 --> 01:34:59,858
Jesus sent me back down here

968
01:35:00,651 --> 01:35:03,654
to save you from the plague
and what lies beyond.

969
01:35:04,237 --> 01:35:06,239
The eternal flames of hell.

970
01:35:06,490 --> 01:35:09,618
Concern yourself
not with the fires of hell.

971
01:35:09,702 --> 01:35:13,121
It may be the fires of this world
that consume you.

972
01:35:14,289 --> 01:35:16,500
Black Death approaches Pescia.

973
01:35:16,875 --> 01:35:18,919
He waits, sharpening his scythe.

974
01:35:19,002 --> 01:35:21,046
I saw swollen bodies. I saw blood.

975
01:35:21,129 --> 01:35:23,381
Rich and poor, women and children.

976
01:35:24,424 --> 01:35:26,134
But Jesus was there too.

977
01:35:27,260 --> 01:35:30,180
He swore that as long as I live,
you shall live!

978
01:35:31,724 --> 01:35:34,101
You stand accused of blasphemy,

979
01:35:34,184 --> 01:35:36,770
heresy and bestiality.

980
01:35:38,731 --> 01:35:40,608
Your trial will begin tomorrow.

981
01:36:06,008 --> 01:36:08,301
We found nothing, your Excellency.

982
01:36:09,803 --> 01:36:11,221
You searched everywhere?

983
01:36:11,304 --> 01:36:13,140
Gutted the mattresses and cushions?

984
01:36:13,223 --> 01:36:15,058
Yes, your Excellency. Nothing.

985
01:36:17,227 --> 01:36:18,436
It's that big.

986
01:36:19,271 --> 01:36:21,524
It must be somewhere. Look again.

987
01:36:23,984 --> 01:36:25,528
What will you tell them?

988
01:36:25,736 --> 01:36:27,112
The truth, what else?

989
01:36:27,780 --> 01:36:29,322
You can tell them something else.

990
01:36:38,582 --> 01:36:40,333
Novice Bartolomea, stand up.

991
01:36:43,962 --> 01:36:44,922
Stand up!

992
01:36:50,052 --> 01:36:51,011
Good.

993
01:36:51,428 --> 01:36:54,222
Sister Felicita, tell us what you saw.

994
01:36:56,058 --> 01:36:58,060
I have no words for such acts.

995
01:36:58,561 --> 01:36:59,853
Do your best.

996
01:37:03,315 --> 01:37:05,901
I saw this girl in carnal embrace

997
01:37:06,902 --> 01:37:08,904
with Mother Superior Benedetta.

998
01:37:10,072 --> 01:37:12,115
Can you be more specific, sister?

999
01:37:13,784 --> 01:37:15,703
They used each other,

1000
01:37:17,120 --> 01:37:18,288
by turns,

1001
01:37:19,498 --> 01:37:20,999
as a man uses a woman.

1002
01:37:22,417 --> 01:37:25,128
How did you come to witness these acts?

1003
01:37:26,505 --> 01:37:28,799
Through a spy hole that I cut myself

1004
01:37:28,882 --> 01:37:31,009
in the wall of my former chamber.

1005
01:37:31,093 --> 01:37:33,095
Is that not a mortal sin?

1006
01:37:33,512 --> 01:37:35,055
Spying on her mother superior.

1007
01:37:35,138 --> 01:37:38,141
We are not judging
the former abbess's conduct.

1008
01:37:38,225 --> 01:37:41,394
We should.
How do we know her declarations

1009
01:37:41,479 --> 01:37:43,105
are not born of jealousy?

1010
01:37:43,188 --> 01:37:45,733
- Or spite?
- Sister Felicita's testimony

1011
01:37:45,816 --> 01:37:47,485
is a beginning not an end.

1012
01:37:48,318 --> 01:37:49,277
Bartolomea...

1013
01:37:50,613 --> 01:37:53,031
how do you respond to this accusation?

1014
01:37:53,741 --> 01:37:55,117
Is there truth in it?

1015
01:37:56,368 --> 01:37:58,411
- I didn't understand.
- Pardon me?

1016
01:37:58,787 --> 01:38:01,081
I didn't understand what she said.

1017
01:38:01,457 --> 01:38:05,002
Have you looked
upon Abbess Benedetta with lust?

1018
01:38:05,085 --> 01:38:06,086
Lust?

1019
01:38:06,169 --> 01:38:08,088
Between women?
Impossible!

1020
01:38:08,171 --> 01:38:11,174
This convent seems rarely bound
by the possible.

1021
01:38:12,300 --> 01:38:13,385
Bartolomea,

1022
01:38:13,969 --> 01:38:18,390
yes or no, have you looked
upon Abbess Benedetta with lust?

1023
01:38:22,352 --> 01:38:23,311
With love.

1024
01:38:26,106 --> 01:38:29,067
All I feel for Mother Benedetta is love.

1025
01:38:30,318 --> 01:38:32,530
The love I feel for all my sisters.

1026
01:38:32,946 --> 01:38:36,534
You have not expressed your love
for your sisters

1027
01:38:36,617 --> 01:38:38,285
in the same way, have you?

1028
01:38:38,368 --> 01:38:39,327
No!

1029
01:38:40,663 --> 01:38:41,830
Sister Felicita,

1030
01:38:42,164 --> 01:38:43,707
by what means

1031
01:38:44,166 --> 01:38:48,921
did novice Bartolomea express
her love for the mother superior?

1032
01:38:52,257 --> 01:38:55,218
She used a wooden figure

1033
01:38:55,302 --> 01:38:56,887
of the Blessed Virgin

1034
01:38:57,805 --> 01:38:59,056
to penetrate

1035
01:38:59,973 --> 01:39:02,350
the sex of Benedetta
and bring her to crisis.

1036
01:39:04,061 --> 01:39:05,646
<i>Crimen nefastum.</i>

1037
01:39:07,523 --> 01:39:10,317
A sacrilegious inversion of natural order.

1038
01:39:10,400 --> 01:39:13,987
An abomination that merits
the ultimate punishment.

1039
01:39:14,905 --> 01:39:15,864
The stake!

1040
01:39:16,364 --> 01:39:17,407
It's not true.

1041
01:39:17,866 --> 01:39:18,909
Not true.

1042
01:39:22,830 --> 01:39:26,124
You might yet save your soul, child.

1043
01:39:27,250 --> 01:39:28,586
If you confess.

1044
01:39:35,383 --> 01:39:37,636
I have nothing to confess,
your Excellency.

1045
01:39:49,106 --> 01:39:51,650
If you know, why must I confess?

1046
01:39:51,734 --> 01:39:53,611
Confession mitigates your sins.

1047
01:39:53,694 --> 01:39:57,114
You might save yourself from the stake.
Benedetta, too.

1048
01:40:24,266 --> 01:40:25,267
Undress her.

1049
01:40:56,840 --> 01:40:59,677
You can save your soul if you speak.

1050
01:41:02,763 --> 01:41:04,014
All right.

1051
01:41:08,477 --> 01:41:09,562
I confess.

1052
01:41:10,312 --> 01:41:11,980
I've had horrible thoughts.

1053
01:41:13,440 --> 01:41:16,485
Sister Juliana is hateful.
I wished her dead!

1054
01:41:16,569 --> 01:41:17,861
Let me go now!

1055
01:41:23,534 --> 01:41:24,535
My child...

1056
01:41:25,243 --> 01:41:26,995
that's not what we want.

1057
01:41:42,595 --> 01:41:43,762
The pear of anguish.

1058
01:41:47,307 --> 01:41:50,227
Have you seen the like before?

1059
01:41:54,231 --> 01:41:56,942
Joan of Arc was a courageous warrior,

1060
01:41:57,025 --> 01:41:59,152
which even her enemies acknowledged,

1061
01:42:00,278 --> 01:42:01,238
and yet,

1062
01:42:01,572 --> 01:42:05,325
she confessed to all her sins
upon sight of the torture instruments.

1063
01:42:07,244 --> 01:42:10,623
There is no need to pretend
to be braver than Joan of Arc.

1064
01:42:11,373 --> 01:42:13,208
No need to pretend anything.

1065
01:42:14,877 --> 01:42:16,378
I've already confessed.

1066
01:42:17,963 --> 01:42:20,466
I told you
I wanted to kill Sister Juliana.

1067
01:42:20,549 --> 01:42:22,175
I am guilty of murder.

1068
01:42:24,177 --> 01:42:25,262
Have mercy.

1069
01:42:40,736 --> 01:42:42,029
I've confessed!

1070
01:42:48,368 --> 01:42:52,039
We are strangers as yet
but we're on the same boat.

1071
01:42:53,791 --> 01:42:55,208
The journey may be long.

1072
01:42:55,751 --> 01:42:57,044
It may be short.

1073
01:42:58,128 --> 01:43:00,130
Let's pray God lights our way.

1074
01:43:57,062 --> 01:43:58,021
Enter!

1075
01:44:09,575 --> 01:44:11,577
What do you think love is?

1076
01:44:17,290 --> 01:44:18,375
I think

1077
01:44:19,292 --> 01:44:21,336
love is not feeling alone.

1078
01:44:23,380 --> 01:44:24,339
It's...

1079
01:44:24,923 --> 01:44:26,008
a warmth here.

1080
01:44:30,345 --> 01:44:31,680
Your feet are sore?

1081
01:44:43,942 --> 01:44:46,487
The abbess would wash my feet?

1082
01:44:49,072 --> 01:44:51,659
As a novice,
I washed more than my share.

1083
01:44:54,620 --> 01:44:56,580
You have never touched a man?

1084
01:44:57,998 --> 01:44:59,249
No.

1085
01:44:59,332 --> 01:45:00,459
Why?

1086
01:45:00,543 --> 01:45:03,170
You don't feel
a woman's natural desires?

1087
01:45:04,588 --> 01:45:06,507
My only desire is for God.

1088
01:45:17,851 --> 01:45:20,353
Trying to seduce me?

1089
01:45:20,437 --> 01:45:22,022
Where'd you pick up a whore's talents?

1090
01:45:22,690 --> 01:45:25,025
I know little of a whore's talents.

1091
01:45:25,108 --> 01:45:27,861
And I won't ask
how you came to know them.

1092
01:45:45,253 --> 01:45:47,465
Play with me, play with fire.

1093
01:45:48,298 --> 01:45:49,382
Literally.

1094
01:45:50,509 --> 01:45:51,594
I'm not afraid.

1095
01:45:52,928 --> 01:45:53,929
Of course.

1096
01:45:55,263 --> 01:45:57,725
You advance,
wearing armor of light.

1097
01:45:58,726 --> 01:46:00,769
Love is the only armor I need.

1098
01:46:01,394 --> 01:46:03,731
The love of Christ, do you mean?

1099
01:46:04,397 --> 01:46:06,108
Or the love of Bartolomea?

1100
01:46:08,235 --> 01:46:09,778
That of Bartolomea also.

1101
01:46:11,321 --> 01:46:12,948
So Jesus must share?

1102
01:46:15,493 --> 01:46:17,495
He joyfully shares everything.

1103
01:46:17,953 --> 01:46:19,412
With the whole human race.

1104
01:46:21,457 --> 01:46:22,833
That warmth you feel.

1105
01:46:22,916 --> 01:46:23,876
Here.

1106
01:46:25,085 --> 01:46:27,379
It's not love
for the whole human race.

1107
01:46:27,463 --> 01:46:29,172
It's particular, isn't it?

1108
01:46:30,298 --> 01:46:32,175
Bartolomea is the particular.

1109
01:46:32,968 --> 01:46:35,012
Through her, I reach universal love.

1110
01:46:37,598 --> 01:46:41,351
Or the universal reaches you
through a chunk of wood, is that right?

1111
01:46:56,742 --> 01:46:58,577
Stay away from me!

1112
01:46:59,244 --> 01:47:00,328
Bartolomea...

1113
01:47:00,954 --> 01:47:03,331
I told them how you deceived me.

1114
01:47:04,625 --> 01:47:06,752
How you forced me to sin.

1115
01:47:08,754 --> 01:47:10,506
They put lies in your mouth.

1116
01:47:10,589 --> 01:47:12,550
I won't suffer for you anymore!

1117
01:47:12,883 --> 01:47:13,967
Go to hell!

1118
01:47:14,051 --> 01:47:15,969
Are you ready to confess now?

1119
01:47:26,104 --> 01:47:28,398
Here's the proof you're looking for.

1120
01:47:43,789 --> 01:47:45,916
There is your love, Benedetta.

1121
01:47:52,465 --> 01:47:53,841
<i>Blasphemy!</i>

1122
01:47:54,717 --> 01:47:55,718
<i>Blasphemy!</i>

1123
01:47:56,051 --> 01:47:57,094
<i>You mock!</i>

1124
01:47:57,678 --> 01:48:00,263
<i>You mock my bride
as they mocked me on the cross!</i>

1125
01:48:01,139 --> 01:48:02,432
<i>Sacrilege!</i>

1126
01:48:02,516 --> 01:48:04,518
<i>You have all been judged!</i>

1127
01:48:04,602 --> 01:48:06,604
<i>You, Alfonso Giglioli!</i>

1128
01:48:07,312 --> 01:48:08,939
<i>You have been judged.</i>

1129
01:48:09,022 --> 01:48:10,566
<i>You'll pay for your blasphemy.</i>

1130
01:48:10,858 --> 01:48:13,360
<i>With your blood, black pus,</i>

1131
01:48:13,443 --> 01:48:14,570
<i>and buboes!</i>

1132
01:48:45,225 --> 01:48:46,644
When did it occur?

1133
01:48:46,727 --> 01:48:47,728
An hour ago.

1134
01:48:47,811 --> 01:48:49,146
Not a word of this.

1135
01:48:49,229 --> 01:48:51,940
Put her in the cellar. Post a guard.

1136
01:48:52,024 --> 01:48:53,734
No one enters or leaves.

1137
01:48:54,109 --> 01:48:56,028
Burn everything she touched!

1138
01:49:29,728 --> 01:49:31,271
Hold your head high.

1139
01:49:33,231 --> 01:49:35,943
One thing I learned as a prostitute,

1140
01:49:37,235 --> 01:49:39,655
humiliation doesn't leave a mark.

1141
01:50:18,401 --> 01:50:20,488
Thief! Stop her!

1142
01:50:28,203 --> 01:50:31,289
The people of Pescia
won't let you burn their protector.

1143
01:50:31,373 --> 01:50:33,876
They have no say.
The Church decides.

1144
01:50:33,959 --> 01:50:36,253
And has decided. Sign.

1145
01:50:36,545 --> 01:50:39,590
Nuncio, remember
the child was pledged to Christ...

1146
01:50:39,673 --> 01:50:40,799
Father!

1147
01:50:41,174 --> 01:50:42,676
Consider your job done.

1148
01:50:44,887 --> 01:50:47,264
I feel pity for Benedetta. And love.

1149
01:50:47,347 --> 01:50:50,433
But pity and love
have nothing to do with duty.

1150
01:50:51,477 --> 01:50:53,896
The sentence is mandatory.

1151
01:51:16,376 --> 01:51:17,628
Your Excellency?

1152
01:51:18,378 --> 01:51:19,421
Yes.

1153
01:51:19,505 --> 01:51:21,549
Sister Benedetta has a request.

1154
01:51:22,591 --> 01:51:25,469
She asks to be allowed
to pray with Sister Felicita

1155
01:51:25,553 --> 01:51:27,304
and beg her forgiveness.

1156
01:51:29,264 --> 01:51:30,724
She also asks

1157
01:51:31,475 --> 01:51:33,310
to be carried onto the square

1158
01:51:33,811 --> 01:51:37,189
on a donkey,
like Christ entering Jerusalem.

1159
01:51:41,026 --> 01:51:43,070
For the donkey, no, of course.

1160
01:51:43,612 --> 01:51:47,282
But I will allow
her little scene with Sister Felicita.

1161
01:51:47,365 --> 01:51:51,036
We must all play our roles
to the end, mustn't we?

1162
01:51:52,663 --> 01:51:53,664
Very well.

1163
01:52:04,467 --> 01:52:05,551
You can go.

1164
01:52:18,564 --> 01:52:21,274
Are you happy to see me dying?

1165
01:52:23,401 --> 01:52:25,863
I came to tell you
Jesus's revelations to me.

1166
01:52:28,616 --> 01:52:30,826
Your daughter
waits for you at his side.

1167
01:52:30,909 --> 01:52:32,828
I don't believe a word of it.

1168
01:52:34,955 --> 01:52:37,958
But she's not in hell.
That's something.

1169
01:52:42,588 --> 01:52:45,799
You gave your life to God
without ever believing in him.

1170
01:52:46,884 --> 01:52:49,052
Now, when he should be your comfort

1171
01:52:49,261 --> 01:52:50,262
and salvation,

1172
01:52:51,221 --> 01:52:53,724
you are alone
facing the terror of death.

1173
01:52:57,435 --> 01:53:00,272
God never spoke to me
the way he speaks to you.

1174
01:53:01,231 --> 01:53:03,066
He speaks to you at this moment.

1175
01:53:04,359 --> 01:53:06,487
He speaks to you through your pain.

1176
01:53:11,534 --> 01:53:13,201
He's very eloquent then.

1177
01:53:15,746 --> 01:53:17,998
But I've no idea what he's telling me.

1178
01:53:22,628 --> 01:53:23,671
What is it?

1179
01:53:24,963 --> 01:53:26,757
What is he telling you?

1180
01:53:29,134 --> 01:53:30,427
You believe that I know?

1181
01:53:31,762 --> 01:53:32,805
Perhaps, yes.

1182
01:53:35,015 --> 01:53:36,517
Yes, you know.

1183
01:53:38,018 --> 01:53:38,977
Yes.

1184
01:53:43,566 --> 01:53:44,650
Tell me.

1185
01:53:47,319 --> 01:53:48,445
Tell me.

1186
01:54:12,260 --> 01:54:13,554
Forgive me!

1187
01:54:17,390 --> 01:54:18,601
Look at me!

1188
01:54:19,017 --> 01:54:20,811
Forgive me! Please!

1189
01:54:21,812 --> 01:54:23,564
Tell me you don't hate me.

1190
01:54:24,773 --> 01:54:26,984
It's fine. I had to be betrayed.

1191
01:54:33,115 --> 01:54:34,533
Death to the nuncio!

1192
01:54:53,552 --> 01:54:54,887
Release her!

1193
01:55:03,061 --> 01:55:04,271
Let me go!

1194
01:55:11,987 --> 01:55:14,698
I grant you the mercy of strangulation.

1195
01:55:14,782 --> 01:55:16,617
You will not endure the flames,

1196
01:55:16,700 --> 01:55:18,368
but make a full confession.

1197
01:55:21,914 --> 01:55:23,874
Renounce your vanity!

1198
01:55:25,042 --> 01:55:26,001
Confess!

1199
01:55:33,258 --> 01:55:34,468
I shall confess.

1200
01:55:39,014 --> 01:55:40,015
Speak!

1201
01:55:48,857 --> 01:55:50,859
Poor city of Pescia!

1202
01:55:52,360 --> 01:55:53,821
I could not save you.

1203
01:55:55,363 --> 01:55:56,907
Or make you renounce wickedness.

1204
01:56:08,752 --> 01:56:10,087
<i>You betrayed my love!</i>

1205
01:56:12,590 --> 01:56:14,883
<i>None of you will be spared!</i>

1206
01:56:15,843 --> 01:56:17,678
<i>Death will run through the town,</i>

1207
01:56:17,761 --> 01:56:20,347
<i>like a wind
scything down all in its path.</i>

1208
01:56:25,769 --> 01:56:26,895
<i>Behold!</i>

1209
01:56:28,313 --> 01:56:31,233
<i>The angel of death
has stretched out her hands.</i>

1210
01:56:32,442 --> 01:56:33,611
<i>Death is here.</i>

1211
01:56:34,903 --> 01:56:37,197
<i>Death walks among you already.</i>

1212
01:56:39,074 --> 01:56:40,283
<i>Angel of death!</i>

1213
01:56:41,494 --> 01:56:42,870
<i>Show your face!</i>

1214
01:56:57,009 --> 01:56:58,176
He did this to me!

1215
01:56:59,970 --> 01:57:01,054
The nuncio!

1216
01:57:02,473 --> 01:57:04,725
He has brought the plague to Pescia.

1217
01:57:05,643 --> 01:57:06,685
Upon you!

1218
01:57:07,144 --> 01:57:08,270
And your children!

1219
01:57:08,353 --> 01:57:09,354
Enough!

1220
01:57:10,022 --> 01:57:11,189
To the stake!

1221
01:57:12,024 --> 01:57:13,400
Take her to the stake!

1222
01:57:14,067 --> 01:57:15,277
To the stake!

1223
01:57:29,082 --> 01:57:31,877
If she dies, we shall all be cursed!

1224
01:57:32,377 --> 01:57:33,420
It's the nuncio!

1225
01:57:33,712 --> 01:57:35,881
The nuncio has brought death to us!

1226
01:57:36,715 --> 01:57:38,634
It's the nuncio who must burn!

1227
01:57:49,352 --> 01:57:51,689
To death! To death!

1228
01:58:20,468 --> 01:58:21,594
Untie her!

1229
01:58:37,485 --> 01:58:38,443
Flee!

1230
01:58:51,499 --> 01:58:52,750
The kiss of peace!

1231
01:59:00,007 --> 01:59:01,258
Catch him!

1232
02:00:10,786 --> 02:00:12,580
Shall I pray for your soul?

1233
02:00:15,874 --> 02:00:17,125
When you died,

1234
02:00:18,210 --> 02:00:19,628
you saw the other world?

1235
02:00:20,337 --> 02:00:22,631
Jesus showed me the place of every soul,

1236
02:00:22,715 --> 02:00:24,800
past, present and to come.

1237
02:00:25,759 --> 02:00:26,760
And me?

1238
02:00:27,886 --> 02:00:30,013
Did you see me in paradise or hell?

1239
02:00:32,766 --> 02:00:33,809
Paradise.

1240
02:00:38,522 --> 02:00:40,398
To the end, you lie.

1241
02:02:15,911 --> 02:02:17,329
What are you doing?

1242
02:02:17,913 --> 02:02:19,081
I must go back.

1243
02:02:23,711 --> 02:02:25,212
There's nothing left there.

1244
02:02:27,422 --> 02:02:29,842
- Why go back?
- The convent's my home.

1245
02:02:29,925 --> 02:02:31,677
I swore to live out my days there.

1246
02:02:31,885 --> 02:02:33,261
That's all in the past.

1247
02:02:34,847 --> 02:02:35,931
Not for me.

1248
02:02:39,727 --> 02:02:41,854
We can go where we want now.

1249
02:02:41,937 --> 02:02:43,939
- You think?
- Yes, anywhere.

1250
02:02:44,022 --> 02:02:46,775
We can go to Rome, Venice, Spain...

1251
02:02:47,400 --> 02:02:48,777
How would we eat?

1252
02:02:49,444 --> 02:02:50,488
By stealing?

1253
02:02:51,029 --> 02:02:51,989
Selling ourselves?

1254
02:02:55,451 --> 02:02:57,911
There's worse.
At least you'd be alive.

1255
02:02:59,204 --> 02:03:01,832
Go back,
and you go back to the stake.

1256
02:03:03,792 --> 02:03:05,335
They won't burn me.

1257
02:03:06,712 --> 02:03:08,046
I'll be protected.

1258
02:03:09,798 --> 02:03:12,217
By who? Your husband Jesus?

1259
02:03:13,385 --> 02:03:15,137
You still don't believe in me?

1260
02:03:15,721 --> 02:03:17,347
After all you've seen?

1261
02:03:17,430 --> 02:03:18,431
Look.

1262
02:03:25,188 --> 02:03:26,732
I've already explained.

1263
02:03:26,815 --> 02:03:28,609
- God possesses me and...
- Stop!

1264
02:03:28,692 --> 02:03:30,152
We're alone. Admit it!

1265
02:03:30,235 --> 02:03:32,780
These stigmata are all stories.
Say it!

1266
02:03:35,574 --> 02:03:36,534
Say it.

1267
02:03:42,831 --> 02:03:44,625
If you care about me, say it.

1268
02:03:48,712 --> 02:03:49,797
Say it!

1269
02:03:49,880 --> 02:03:51,882
Why make me say atrocities?

1270
02:03:51,965 --> 02:03:53,551
I don't want you to die.

1271
02:03:56,720 --> 02:04:00,057
The people behind you yesterday
will throw you to the flames.

1272
02:04:06,104 --> 02:04:07,105
You're right.

1273
02:04:09,650 --> 02:04:11,234
They'll tie me to the stake.

1274
02:04:12,319 --> 02:04:13,654
They'll set it on fire.

1275
02:04:15,489 --> 02:04:18,075
The flames will touch me
but will not burn me.

1276
02:04:19,284 --> 02:04:20,661
God won't let them.

1277
02:04:22,204 --> 02:04:23,371
And all will see.

1278
02:04:24,582 --> 02:04:26,625
No one will doubt ever again.

1279
02:04:26,709 --> 02:04:29,795
You will never doubt
or fear anything again.

1280
02:04:30,546 --> 02:04:32,214
That will be my gift to you.

1281
02:04:34,842 --> 02:04:37,094
You are mad. Mad.

1282
02:04:40,097 --> 02:04:41,849
You're a child, Bartolomea.

1283
02:04:42,558 --> 02:04:44,351
And that's part of your charm.

1284
02:04:53,151 --> 02:04:54,111
Go!

1285
02:04:55,863 --> 02:04:57,030
Go then!

1286
02:04:58,115 --> 02:04:59,575
Go to the devil!

1287
02:05:01,702 --> 02:05:03,328
I hope he burns you!

1288
02:05:06,081 --> 02:05:07,165
Go!

1289
02:05:33,358 --> 02:05:37,738
Sister Benedetta was denied martyrdom.

1290
02:05:37,821 --> 02:05:43,368
She lived to the age of 70,
confined in the convent of the Theatines.

1291
02:05:43,452 --> 02:05:48,624
She was permitted to attend mass
and on occasion to dine with her sisters,

1292
02:05:48,707 --> 02:05:51,794
seated on the floor.

1293
02:05:53,796 --> 02:05:58,842
The plague ravaging the country
completely spared Pescia.
